'''4.''' ''pl.'' The inner parts as the seat of pity or kindness; hence, tenderness; compassion.
{{smaller block|He that relieves another upon the bare suggestion and ''bowels'' of pity, doth not this so much for his sake as for his own.
{{right|''Sir T. Browne'', Religio Medici, ii. 2.}}}}
